everyone loves a good Easter it unless  you're lactose-intolerant  in which case pop culture Easter eggs  are a fading substitute Easter eggs are  those little nuggets of fanservice show  creators include for those fans with  waiting way too much time on their hands  and wouldn't you know it my hands are  covered in time right now so enter  Dragon Ball super whether you love it or  hate it this little series has jammed  itself full of obscure and some not so  obscure references to its parent show  Dragon Ball Z as well as the occasional  pop culture reference or two what's that  don't believe me well you're in luck  because today I'm bringing you the 15  best Dragon Ball super  Easter eggs number 15 Dragon Balls  walking punchline otherwise known as  Yamcha since his cremation at the hands  of a Cyberman in the late 80s has thanks  to the internet reached maximum meme  capacity you can even get a freaking  statue of his death  clearly Toei was in on the joke too  because in episode 70 of Dragon Ball  super otherwise known as the baseball  episode young Jeff finds himself  completely physically mismatched with  the likes of Vegeta on the opposite team  filled with nods to dr. slump it's clear  to see that this episode is purely a  gift for the fans the episode reaches a  satisfying climax with Yamcha assuming  his most famous pose a cheeky nod to any  longtime fans of the series only this  time instead of it resulting in his  death he reaches home base winning the  game for his team  fantastic moment and awesome to see  Yamcha finally get a win  go yaaaa number 14 I don't particularly  like to talk about a kid looking for  tail often or at all really but episode  88 of Dragon Ball super made me do just  that thinking back to the Saiyan saga of  Dragon Ball Z many fans would remember  kid go on chasing a certain dinosaur  hoping to slice off a portion of its  tail to cook for dinner  fast-forward to Dragon Ball super as  piccolo and Gohan train in preparation  for the tournament of power they decide  to spend some time together in a very  nostalgic familiar setting I just hope  it wasn't the same dinosaur poor thing  hardly had any tail as it was number 13  this one I almost missed entirely it  goes by quite fast sticking with the  same arc we land on episode 76 as Goku  and krillen take on an army of  villainous illusions in a forest with  just the most inviting name backed into  a corner by an imposing illusion of  nappa Crillon pulls a Crillon by kicking  nappa square in the jaw and yeah that's  totally pulling a Crillon because he  nails him with the exact same  he did in the saying sock a lot of these  are references to the say in saga I'm  noticing number 12  sticking with the cruel man himself we  arrived in episode 20 smack dab in the  middle of the Resurrection earth park  you know everyone's favorite in this  episode Bulma attempts to gather the Z  warriors in preparation for the  impending arrival of Frieza  and so while chatting with Crillon this  happens do you hear that if that sounds  familiar then you must be a one-piece  fan or at least Crillon is because that  ringtone is a theme song from one piece  fun fact the Japanese voice of Crillon  is also the Japanese voice of Luffy from  one piece number 11 you know Mosca was  always the god destruction I liked least  it could have been his doofy voice can't  wait for the English dub of that one his  weird arms or maybe a combination of the  two I could never quite put my finger on  why turns out Moscow is their  amalgamation of a shitty GD character  called lute just look he's taken his  eyes that stupid belly button plate  thing he has the exact same hands pretty  much everything down to the color is  copied from this character all this time  I wondered why I didn't like Moscow and  it turns out it's because he looks like  a fat guy and shitty GT cosplay number  10 with the commencement of episode 77  so too came the beginning of a brand new  arc we pick up with Goku who by all  accounts is doing great work actually  cashing in on the crops he produced  since the ending of the Future Trunks  arc he seems to be doing quite well for  himself  however on his way back from the market  he gets ambushed by some thugs looking  to rob him in response Goku does this  [Music]  look familiar well it should because  this exact same thing happened at the  beginning of Dragon Ball Z with his  brother Raddatz you know what they say  like brother like brother that doesn't  sound right  number 9 episode 30 wasn't exactly the  most exciting episode to watch but it  did have a neat little Easter egg with  majin buu and another Majin you might  not be familiar with you'll see while  Goku Crillon and Vegeta are trying to  convince Buu to join the team to fight  universe 6  Buu is reading a comic and this isn't  some random comic it's one written and  drawn by Akira Toriyama himself entitled  nickel Majin a manga series produced  between 1999 and 2005 number 8 in Dragon  Ball Z when the mysterious super saiyan  from the Future Trunks arrived it took  many a Dragon Ball fan aback though when  Goku arrived he quickly took the wind  out of his sails as Goku tends to do and  if you thought things would be different  in the future trunks arc of Dragon Ball  super a whopping 216 episodes later  you'd be very very wrong once trunks  arrives back in Goku's present timeline  in episode 49 he wants to test his  strength during the confrontation before  Goku does this using only his fingers he  stops trunks his blade right in its  tracks even smiling at him as if to say  that we've been here before haven't we  number 7 swinging right back from  episode 49 to the very first episode of  the series we all remember mr. Satan was  trying to hand over 100 million Zeni to  Goku as a thanks for doing all the work  against majin buu but what you might not  have noticed was the illustration on the  money in the case you see that weird  robot thing right there that's not  random that's actually a drawing Akira  Toriyama would use to depict himself in  the manga series for Dragon Ball he's  plastered all over it good old Tori  bought a really nice nod to the series  creator number 6  sometimes I'm faced with symbolism that  I just can't ignore and while this might  be a bit of a stretch I couldn't help  myself but to include all the same  featured in episode 46 the finale of the  short-lived filler story known as the  boot arc Vegeta is shown to be using a  pacifier to stop his body from fading  away as rapidly as it was if you don't  know the story it's complicated  check it out it's pretty cool but those  images of Vegeta with a pacifier I can't  help but think is a subtle nod to baby  from Dragon Ball GT this would might be  a bit out there but I love it all the  same number 5 fast forward now to a more  recent episode and we find ourselves in  the middle of a clash between ultra  instant Goku and kefla during the  tournament of power in episode 116 apart  from being a fantastic fight from  beginning to end this episode also  featured this moment blitzing forward to  strike Goku Katla's blow misses entirely  while Goku appears to have not moved a  muscle  if this doesn't look familiar to you it  should if you've seen Dragon Ball Z that  is feature towards the end of episode 66  during the Namek saga goku is seen or  should i say not seen dodging an attack  from raccoon  resulting in raccoon regaining his  bounds in a very similar fashion to  kevlar this exchange is too similar to  not be a callback at the very least to  this moment number 4 from a later  episode back to one of the earliest we  find ourselves an episode 2 of super now  there's the obvious Vegeta keeping his  promise to trunks that he made back in Z  I could do but that's too easy  let's look at this word instead through  the intentionally rough path Puma took  to the resort Vegeta atop the roof finds  himself looking a little disheveled to  say the least if you look specifically  at what's in his hair you'll notice two  types of fruit commonly found in Japan  these two fruits being a durian and as a  Bandhan these just so happened to be the  two fruit that czar bon and dodoria were  named after two people Vegeta killed  while on Namek number three the next  three entries on this list are the most  subtle and I love them all the more  forest beginning with this  reintroduction between two one-time foes  Android 17 and piccolo in episode 94 I  wouldn't be surprised if this flew under  the radar for many viewers it did for me  as Android 17 is approaching the capsule  core building he stares down piccolo who  removes his head where in response to  this Android 17 begins to roll up his  sleeve this is mimicking the exact  movements he made before they fought in  episode 148 of Dragon Ball Z it not only  acts as a nice swerve for those in the  audience that picked up on that but also  adds an extra level of psychology to the  script giving more reason as to why  Android 17 looked amused by Piccolo's  peace offering extending his hand number  2  one thing fans might not have noticed  about the ending to resurrection F is  much it mimics the original fight that  took place on Namek except for the  ending but we'll look past that if we  think back to the fighter Namek we  remember Vegeta being shot through the  chest being stomped on laying in a heap  looking for help and Goku's arrival to  lend a hand in the resurrection F fight  the exact same beats are hit in that  order but with the roles reversed goku  gets shot through the chest gets stomped  on is left in a heap looking for help  ultimately leading to vegeta showing up  to aid in the situation this is a subtle  inclusion that I didn't pick up on my  first time viewing but one that makes  the scene all the better when you see  the parallels now before we move on to  the number one spot let's take a look at  some honorable mentions  number one I had to save my favorite for  last episode 94 for many will be  remembered as the episode that had the  best Frieza transformation in the series  but for me it's special for another very  subtle reason while waiting for fortune  teller Baba to return with freezer from  the other world we the viewers see Goku  for the first time in decades outside  her place sparing one would think with  no one however when put side by side you  can clearly see that he is reliving one  of the last times he saw his grandpa  Gohan it's inclusions such as this that  tells me Dragon Ball super has some  fantastic people working behind the  scenes on the show occasionally  sprinkling it with tidbits of history  and lore that we can all appreciate if  we care to look these were my favourite  Easter eggs from Dragon Ball super leave  me know why yours were in the comments  down below did I miss any if you're new  to this channel I upload every week so  feel free to subscribe for more content  such as this as always comments and  ratings are very much appreciated but  that will do it for this week thank you  so much for watching

